      "standardized_narrative": "At 31 December 2021 Syndicate 1861's opening gross claims outstanding (prior year comparative) was GBP 770.971m. Analysis of the gross claims development shows an adverse re-estimate on the 2019 underwriting year of approximately GBP 34.5m (gross), representing a ~4.48% strengthening versus opening gross claims outstanding. Management attributes movements to a mix of factors including natural catastrophe-driven large loss development, some COVID-19 related movements (a favourable GBP 1.3m reported), reinsurance transactions (RITC adjustments and an LPT in December 2021) and recoveries; overall the prior-year movement is an adverse strengthening on the older years.",
